# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Decision OS activation flags (Aug 2026) — committed deliberately.
#
# These are NON-SECRET boolean kill switches (see lib/decision-os/*/shadow.ts
# and lib/decision-os/PRODUCTION_READINESS_CHECKLIST.md). Next.js loads
# .env.production into the server runtime; a variable set in the Vercel
# dashboard ALWAYS takes precedence over this file — so the instant-rollback
# contract survives: set any flag to "false" in Vercel project settings (or
# edit this file) to kill a slice without touching code.
#
# Stage 0 (shadow): each slice runs beside the legacy engine and logs
# [decision-os] parity telemetry. Stage 1 (live): a purely-additive
# `decisionOs` field is appended to the existing API responses. No existing
# behavior changes in either stage; Decision OS never writes to the DB.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Slice 1 — manager.lineup.set (today/lineup-actions + today-actions engine)
DECISION_OS_LINEUP_SHADOW=true
DECISION_OS_LINEUP_LIVE=true

# Slice 2 — manager.waiver.claim (waiver-ai engine response)
DECISION_OS_WAIVER_SHADOW=true
DECISION_OS_WAIVER_LIVE=true

# Slice 3 — manager.trade.evaluate (redraft trade-proposals response)
DECISION_OS_TRADE_SHADOW=true
DECISION_OS_TRADE_LIVE=true

# Slice 4 — commissioner.league.health (commissioner hub payload)
DECISION_OS_COMMISSIONER_HEALTH_SHADOW=true
DECISION_OS_COMMISSIONER_HEALTH_LIVE=true

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-surface TRADE shadow instrumentation (lib/decision-os/trade/surfaceShadow.ts)
#
# DECISION_OS_TRADE_SHADOW above governs the canonical proposal path. These six
# flags cover the ten OTHER places a user can get a trade verdict. They are
# observation-only: each surface keeps rendering its own answer and additionally
# emits a [decision-os] parity event comparing that answer to the canonical value
# engine. Nothing user-facing changes; no DB writes.
#
# They exist because the Phase 3 flip gate (>=95% agreement over >=50 comparisons
# per surface) cannot report "ready" honestly while blind to a surface. The
# legacy analyzer is the highest-traffic trade surface in the product — the
# dashboard "Trade Analyzer" tile routes to /af-legacy, not the console — so
# leaving LEGACY dark would have gated the flip on the least-used path.
#
# Leave these on until each surface has accumulated its sample stream, then
# consult parity telemetry before flipping anything to LIVE.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DECISION_OS_TRADE_SHADOW_CONSOLE=true
DECISION_OS_TRADE_SHADOW_DYNASTY=true
DECISION_OS_TRADE_SHADOW_KEEPER=true
DECISION_OS_TRADE_SHADOW_DRAFTPICK=true
DECISION_OS_TRADE_SHADOW_LEGACY=true
# One flag, five war rooms (redraft/dynasty/keeper/bestball/guillotine) — they
# share a verdict rule but stay distinct surfaces in telemetry because they use
# different value bases, so each converges or diverges on its own.
DECISION_OS_TRADE_SHADOW_WARROOM=true
